FreeWnn source and patch provenance
===================================

This candidate no longer uses the Debian 1.1.1~a021+cvs20130302-8 source
base. The upstream source is the FreeWnn 1.1.1-a023 tarball imported as
1.1.1~a023 and recorded by reference/a023-base. The historical Debian
packaging VCS through revision -5 is at reference/debian-packaging-2015;
the imported -8 packaging is at debian/1.1.1_a021+cvs20130302-8. The GCC
14/15 and C23 compatibility work is at reference/gcc15-main-20260711.

Historical Debian patch disposition
------------------------------------

* newlayout was empty and is dropped.
* makerules.mk.in is replaced by 1000-debian-filesystem-layout.patch.
* man is split into 1001-fix-manpage-sections.patch and
  1002-escape-hyphen-in-atod-manpage.patch.
* hardening-flags is dropped because a023 propagates CPPFLAGS and LDFLAGS.
* hurd_support.patch is refreshed as 0050-define-MAXPATHLEN-fallback.patch.
* fix-parallel-build.patch is dropped because a023 has the fixed dependency.
* egrep-a.patch is superseded by
  0005-build-dictionaries-in-C-locale.patch.
* implicit_functions.diff from -8 is replaced by the logical configure,
  system-declaration, and prototype patches in this series.

The patch-relevant -5 to -8 delta was: two DEP-3 fields added to
egrep-a.patch; implicit_functions.diff added for Debian bug #1065772; and
its series entry added. Other packaging changes are outside this task.

Mixed source commit mapping
---------------------------

* a85b88729c2fa7d0a2ec542d737c5e19061c8a47: sort callbacks -> 0020;
  jl_dic_add_e handlers -> 0022.
* 17578cf34877cad67c465335afbf499b88cecce1: getopt -> 0011; redundant
  bdic declarations -> 0012.
* 915ecd5efe7a9ab09fc073c8131687184a45dfa4: internal sort interface ->
  0020; direct qsort comparators -> 0021; jl_dic_add_e callbacks -> 0022;
  other internal callbacks -> 0023; byte-buffer types -> 0025.
* 9618769b8e758f537db180a9389c7ce10c536163: redundant declarations ->
  0012; internal helpers -> 0023; signal handlers -> 0030; variadic out ->
  0031.
* 3cc4bf1f5fd9178741dd904612f2110a9470e86b: byte-buffer signedness ->
  0025; the functional wnn_sStrncpy conversion-direction fix -> 0040.

The GCC reference also removes redundant jutil declarations in
4cf1f77f2e20b8540aaf8e9478ba6e440dff2a78. They have the exact purpose of
0012 and are recorded there to preserve the verified GCC reference tree.

Generated configure policy
--------------------------

Only configure.in changes are carried. Generated configure is excluded,
including d2ce32b7afd3d79e810c08051c937106cbdf1332 and the configure half of
b8c95ad64da5de58857c72f4b3644d90c6e6e53c. Regenerate it with autoreconf.

Testing
-------

Run `debian/codex/tools/verify-task01.sh` from a clean source tree. It checks
the exact series, whitespace, generated-configure exclusion, quilt
application, the detailed GCC-reference comparison, autoreconf, and a
parallel GNU C23 build.

Unresolved work
---------------

This task does not modernize general Debian packaging, complete copyright
or policy review, establish an adopter or maintainer, or demonstrate upload
readiness. Those require later human decisions and review.
